## 4. Is the record a useful architectural instrument?

**Yes — plainly useful, even though not formally acceptable.** It is the first revision
whose consumer inventory matches the code (I found zero omissions where v2 had five);
its negative inventory (the four re-derivations + the 2689 fallback, all with verified
lines) is itself a concrete, reusable artifact for whoever next attacks the P08
acceptance criteria; the JOIN PRECONDITION statement is the first place the
load-bearing join invariant is written down at all (no prior document stated it); and
the DRAFT/§7/§8 framing — claims scoped, non-proofs disclaimed, acceptance bar explicit
— is exactly the posture the process asked for after two NOT-ACCEPTABLE verdicts. v2 was
misleading (false structural claims, incomplete inventory); this version is honest and
